# WHITELIST .gitignore — read AGENTS.md before editing.
#
# Everything is ignored by default. A file can only be committed if it matches
# one of the `!` patterns below. This makes it impossible to accidentally commit
# game assets, extracted data, exported meshes/images, or build output.
#
# To allow a new kind of file, add the narrowest pattern that works and mention
# it in your change summary. Never add broad patterns like `!*` or `!**/*`.
# Never whitelist binary formats (.bin, .png, .obj, .assets, .bundle, ...).

# 1. Ignore everything.
*

# 2. Let git descend into directories (files inside are still ignored unless
#    whitelisted below).
!*/

# 3. Repository metadata and project docs.
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/AGENTS.md
!/README.md
!/MODLOG.md
!/STATUS.md
!/LICENSE-MIT
!/LICENSE-APACHE
!/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
!/docs/**/*.md

# 4. Rust workspace configuration.
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/rust-toolchain.toml
!/rustfmt.toml
!/clippy.toml
!/deny.toml
!/.cargo/config.toml

# 5. Our source code. Only Rust sources, manifests and our own WGSL shaders.
!/crates/*/Cargo.toml
!/crates/*/README.md
!/crates/*/src/**/*.rs
!/crates/*/src/**/*.wgsl
!/crates/*/tests/**/*.rs
!/crates/*/benches/**/*.rs
!/crates/*/examples/**/*.rs
!/apps/*/Cargo.toml
!/apps/*/README.md
!/apps/*/src/**/*.rs
!/apps/*/src/**/*.wgsl
!/apps/*/tests/**/*.rs

# 6. CI.
!/.github/workflows/*.yml

# 7. Hard re-ignores. These win over everything above because they come last.
#    Build output, local game copies, extraction/export scratch space, and the
#    third-party guides folder that lives next to the repo.
/target/
/out/
/game/
/extracted/
/scratch/
/ai-game-modding-guides-main/
